55,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"Option A is paid allocation, B is shared racks, and C is an annual lottery.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"Shared racks sound flexible, but I worry about the rain and the shoving.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,May,,Paid allocation is perfect. It brings in money and rewards those who actually use the bikes.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,George,,Shared racks with double-tier frames sound like a maintenance nightmare. I dislike Option A's paperwork.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Mio,,"A lottery is fair, but the daily riders would prefer to pay for a guaranteed spot.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"A lottery is the most neutral. It prevents the ""permanent"" spots Mio mentioned.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Shizue,,But a lottery every year might be stressful for some.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,May,,"@George, if you hate the paperwork, maybe we can simplify it? Option A is the most logical.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,George,,I prefer the lottery. It's a one-time event per year. Very low maintenance.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Misaki, would a lottery stop the leaning bike complaints?","{""words"":9,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"It might, as people would be more mindful of a spot they won.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Shizue,,I think the lottery is the gentlest way to ensure everyone has a chance.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,May,,It's a waste of potential revenue. I'm sticking with the paid model.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,George,,I'm voting for the lottery. It's the only one that doesn't create a permanent chore.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Mio,,"I'm torn, but the lottery is definitely fairer than the current situation.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,4,talk,Misaki,,I agree. The lottery preserves the peace.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,4,talk,Shizue,,I will vote for the lottery as well.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,4,talk,May,,I'll stay with Option A.,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,4,talk,George,,My choice is firm.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,4,talk,Mio,,I'll go with the lottery too.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
